(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment regarding the prevalence of substance abuse among youth in Jammu and Kashmir;
(b) the district-wise number of persons treated for drug addiction during the last five years;
(c) the number of Government-run de-addiction centres presently functional; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen prevention, treatment and rehabilitation services?

(a) weather Government is aware of inordinate delays, repeated revisions and cost escalations in the implementing of Smart City Mission (SCM) projects in Srinagar and Jammu;
(b) the project wise details of sanctioned cost, revised cost, original completion date, present status and reason for delay;
(c) weather any inquiry, audit or investigation has been initiated into alleged financial irregularities, poor work quality execution, diversion of funds or lapses in project management and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the total funds released and utilized so far, the names of defaulting contractors/agencies, penalties imposed and the revised timeline for completion of all pending projects?

(a) the status of implementation of the Jammu and Kashmir Industrial Policy, including investment proposals approved, grounded and operational;
(b) the details of incentives, subsidies and land allotted to industrial units during the last five year, project-wise; and
(c) the number of projects cancelled, delayed or found non-operational after availing Government incentives, along with action taken to recover public funds and whether any independent audit has been conducted to verify actual employment generation against investment commitments, if so, the findings thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of mental health disorders arising out of prolonged conflict, natural disasters and substance abuse in Jammu and Kashmir;
(b) the number of psychiatrists, psychologists and counsellors available in Government institutions;
(c) the availability of mental health facilities, district-wise; and
(d) the steps taken to expand such services?

(a) the original sanctioned cost and completion schedule of Pakal Dul, Kiru, Kwar and Retlay projects vis-a-vis current estimated cost and revised schedule;
(b) the extent to which cloudburst/floods damage has been cited to justify missed deadline, with documentary basis of each instance, project-wise; and
(c) weather escalation is attributable to genuine natural causes or fund diversions/deviations under other heads and a project-wise statements of such diversions/deviations, if any?

(a) the detailed status of current Drug Users in UT of J and K, substance-wise;
(b) total quantity of narcotics and psychotropic substances seized during last five years, substances-wise details thereof;
(c) age-wise and district-wise details of drug addiction cases, number of NDPS cases registered, persons arrested and convictions secured;
(d) details of rehabilitation centres, de-addiction facilities, counselling programmes, current capacities and details of staff and consultants engaged with these facilities, district-wise and further road map; and
(e) steps taken by Government to prevent the smugglings of drugs in J and K?

(a) the details of frauds detected or reported in J&K Bank, amount involved, FIRs registered and officials held accountable since 2021, year-wise;
(b) the total employees recruited, regularised or engaged on contract post 2019 by following recruitment process in the bank;
(c) the total loans sanctioned, outstanding amount and growth, sector-wise; 
(d) the total value of default by top 100 defaulters, NPA-wise; 
(e) the details of one time settlements, restructuring, write-offs and loan waivers approved for beneficiaries, amount recovery effected, pending dues; and
(f) the corrective, supervisory and penal actions taken to safeguard money and depositors interests?

(a) the present legal status, notified areas, boundary demarcation and management plan of Kishtwar High Altitude National Park;
(b) the details of biodiversity including flagship species such as snow leopard, prey base, threatened flora and fauna and results of recent scientific surveys; and
(c) steps taken for habitat protection, anti poaching and climate change adaptation, human conflicts, livestock depredation compensations and grazing regulation, involvement and livelihood support of local and nomadic communities, tourism policy, carrying capacity and waste management, availability of funds, staff strength and inter-agency coordination and future plans for corridor conservation, research, eco-development and transparent public reporting?

(a) the university-wise details of appointment of the Vice-Chancellors in all Central, State and Semi Government Universities in Jammu and Kashmir during last three years;
(b) the statutory provisions and eligibility criteria followed, composition of search-cum-selection committees, number of applications received, candidates shortlisted and interviewed and final basis of selection; and
(c) how many shortlisted candidates were domiciles of Jammu and Kashmir and how many were from outside the UT, whether any weightage was given to regional experience and whether the entire process complied with UGC norms?

(a) whether National Health Mission (NHM) employees working for over 18 years in rural and Urban health institutions of Jammu & Kashmir (J&K) continue without any regularization policy, job security or equal wages and steps proposed for their regularization in view of 90:10 central funding of the scheme and Central Government's clarification that regularization falls under the domain of State/UT Government; 
(b) whether J&K UT plans phased absorption of NHM staff on regular posts with a defined roadmap, if not, the reasons therefor; and
(c) whether Government proposes to do away with the pay disparity between NHM staff in the UT and other States?

(a) the present operational status, sanctioned strength, services offered and revised completion timelines of AIIMS, Jammu and AIIMS, Awantipora along with reasons of delays;
(b) the district-wise details of Government Medical Colleges (GMCs) in Jammu & Kashmir, including sanctioned and vacant post of faculty, paramedical  and other staff , MBBS and PG seat capacity, Super specialty services and steps taken to address acute manpower shortage; and
(c) whether Government is considering establishment of new GMCs in uncovered districts of J&K especially Kishtwar, Ramban, Poonch?

(a) whether Government proposes to establish a full fledged passport office or Passport Seva Kendra in Chenab Valley Region of J&K considering the vast geography and public hardships;
(b) the number of passport applications pending in the Union Territory, district-wise, as on date;
(c) the average time taken for processing, police verification and delivery of passports; and
(d) the steps taken to coordinate with concerned authorities to ensure time bound issuance of pending applications?

(a) whether Government has assessed the absence of any full fledged University in the Chenab Region of J&K, comprising Kishtwar, Doda and Ramban Districts, forcing students to migrate to distant regions for higher and postgraduate education;
(b) if so, whether Government proposes to establish a new Multi-disciplinary University in the Chenab Region to address regional imbalance, improve access for students for remote and hilly areas and strength human resources development; and
(c) the details of feasibility studies conducted, land identification, financial implications and timelines, if any?

(a) the present status of Ayushman Bharat - Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY) in J&K, including district-wise data on cards issued, eligible but excluded families, empaneled Government and private hospitals and claims filed, settled and pending along with amounts released to hospitals; 
(b) the reason for issues of Aadhaar/SECC errors, delayed card generation, frequent claims rejections, low package rates, denial of cashless treatment and prolonged reimbursement delays to hospitals; and 
(c) whether the minority would outline a time bound plan to empanel all eligible private hospitals and ensure timely payments and universal coverage?

(a) the reasons as to why permission for 50 MBBS seats was granted to Shri Mata Vaishno Devi Institute of Medical Excellence and admissions allowed to proceed despite subsequent withdrawal by the NMC;
(b) whether Medical Assessment and Rating Board Conducted a full pre-admission inspection and issued requisite clearances before students were admitted, if so, who authorized the initial admissions and who ordered the revocation; and
(c) the specific deficiencies found and what adequate compensation, seat adjustments and safeguards are being provided to protect the educational interests of affected students?

(a) the total revenue earned to date from the operational Dul Hasti Hydroelectric power project, Kishtwar, J and K;
(b) the current status of Dul Hasti Stage II project in term of approval, construction timeline and financial outlay;
(c) whether Government is proceeding with the original commitment for phase II to be executed as a joint venture between NHPC Ltd. and CVPPL or has that arrangement been changed; and
(d) the locals who gave land for Phase I and were promised jobs against that, not yet have been employed, whether they will be considered for jobs in Phase II as part of project benefits?

(a) whether Government proposes to develop the new airstrips/airports in j and k to enhance regional connectivity as well as strategic and defence requirements;
(b) the present status of Kishtwar airstrip, including feasibility studies, land acquisition, security clearance, funding and timeline for completion, weather it is covered under the UDAN scheme and the reasons for delay; and
(c) the measures being taken by Government to curb rising airfares especially in winters on routes to and fro Delhi to Jammu, Delhi to Kashmir and Jammu to Kashmir?

(a) whether Government has any plans, Detailed Project Reports (DPRs) or sanctioned projects to extend railway lines into Chenab valley including Doda, Kishtwar, Bhaderwah, Padder and adjoining areas and into Pir Panjal;
(b) if so, the status of each proposal, timeline, environment and forest clearances and technical challenges identified; 
(c) the funds that have been allocated for feasibility studies or pre-construction works, and the employment and tourism benefits that are expected; and 
(d) by when can these regions expect operational rail connectivity?

(a) the district-wise status of sports infrastructure, coaching staff and funding in J&K; 
(b) the number of playgrounds, indoor halls and hostels sanctioned, completed or pending since 2021; 
(c) the steps taken to ensure transparent selections for scholarships, Khelo India scheme and National Camps; 
(d) the measures taken to revive defunct facilities in rural and border areas and timelines with budgetary allocations to bridge regional disparities, especially in Chenab region; and 
(e) the details  of employment provided since 2021 in the UT to sportsmen, coaches and allied staff, including contractual, district-wise and the pending cases?

(a) the present operational status of AIIMS Jammu which is partially functional and, AIIMS Awantipora in Kashmir, which remains under construction; 
(b) the total sanctioned faculty and non-faculty posts the cadre-wise details of appointments made, the number of existing vacancies and reasons for persistent manpower deficits; 
(c) the departments that are presently fully functional at AIIMS, Jammu and those proposed to be activated first in AIIMS, Awantipora; and 
(d) the projected timelines for full operationalisation of both institutes and whether Government intends to expedite the establishment of newly approved medical colleges in Jammu and Kashmir with assured staffing and infrastructure?
